{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews","id":1083449,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Charm Previews","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-25T07:28:10-07:00","id":1083449,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Charm Previews","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dragon-blooded-charms-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dragon-blooded-charms-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\"> Dragon-Blooded Charms preview! [Exalted] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dragon-blooded-charms-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/dragon-blooded-charms-preview-exalted/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Didn't see a thread for this yet, very interested in what you all think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:04:22-07:00","id":1083455,"title":"","content":"You can see a slight inclination towards Dragonblooded teamwork complementing the essential uses of some of these. That's cool to see. Dragon's Hidden Treasure is a neat charm, and the Essence 3 charms stand out positively in flavor and power. I like the descriptions for all of them, though a few could be bumped up a bit.<br /> <br /> The matching element(s) of each charm being represented by keywords makes sense to me, whatever the eventual benefit might be. Treat them as favored purchases if they match the character's Aspect, I'd guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-25-2017, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:25:36-07:00","id":1083468,"title":"","content":"I'll also throw down that Dragon's Hidden Treasure is a really cool one. Lots of cool stunt fodder in that nifty little Charm.<br /> <br /> And the Spirit Chaining attack is really cool, too, being one of the teamwork Charms. Interesting that it only applies to other Dragon-Bloods...I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:33:45-07:00","id":1083471,"title":"","content":"Hmm, nothing too exciting, IMHO. I'd have certainly liked to see a combat Charm to get a feel for their power level or something else really evocative. Hiding things in stone is a neat trick, but not very flashy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:35:59-07:00","id":1083475,"title":"","content":"I would have liked to see one of their base dice adders, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:54:04-07:00","id":1083481,"title":"","content":"<i>Following the River's Course </i>really puzzles me. Does it only apply to transactions made with hard currency? If not and it also applies to transfers of ledger-wealth...how the heck does the ST decide how they obtained &quot;that&quot; money, exactly? What money, precisely? Money is fungible, and ledger-wealth is even more abstract. If a merchant prince who buys goods from you pays with money he has obtained across a broad array of transactions in different markets, do you learn about <i>all </i>of those transactions, and therefore <i>all </i>of the Intimacies that were upheld while doing so? For that matter, what level of detail is offered here? Do I learn just the goods and services he sold, or do I also learn where, and when, and to whom? What are the boundaries for the knowledge imparted?<br /> <br /> It's a neat idea, but I have a hard time understanding how this would actually work in play.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <i>Reading the Unspoken Word </i>is also a little vague. So...in the example of the guard of a secret meeting, does the Charm reveal that he is expecting to hear <i>a</i> password, or does it also let me know what the password is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":1315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","user":"Ferryman","date":". 04-25-2017, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:13:34-07:00","id":1083488,"title":"","content":"Oh, cool, an anima Charm with a 1a cost. Don't remember offhand if we have any with a less-than-3a cost in the core.<br /> <br /> Is... is Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm actually doing anything? Like, that looks a lot like something you should be able to just <i>do</i> with Survival, i.e., &quot;I'ma roll to find some useful fever-treating herbs that grow in the area, because I have Survival 3+.&quot; I'm kinda underwhelmed there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:20:32-07:00","id":1083492,"title":"","content":"Randomly pulling a lion's den into existence out of nothing but plot isn't something you can do with survival alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:28:47-07:00","id":1083496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083492#post1083492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Randomly pulling a lion's den into existence out of nothing but plot isn't something you can do with survival alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it not? I would probably let a player say, &quot;Hey, can I roll to find a lion's den here in the savannah?&quot; which seems like it functionally comes to the same thing (i.e., if they succeed at a difficulty I set, then yes, suddenly lion dens - which basically are the &quot;declare a fact&quot; rules).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:31:11-07:00","id":1083497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083488#post1083488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, cool, an anima Charm with a 1a cost. Don't remember offhand if we have any with a less-than-3a cost in the core.<br /> <br /> Is... is Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm actually doing anything? Like, that looks a lot like something you should be able to just <i>do</i> with Survival, i.e., &quot;I'ma roll to find some useful fever-treating herbs that grow in the area, because I have Survival 3+.&quot; I'm kinda underwhelmed there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A normal survival roll would go more like<br /> <br /> PC: &quot;I'm rolling to find shelter.&quot;<br /> GM: &quot;Difficulty 3&quot;<br /> PC: &quot;I got 4&quot;<br /> GM: You find a small cave off the beaten track<br /> <br /> Using this charm lets you say:<br /> <br /> PC: &quot;There's a large cave surrounded by an orchard that's more or less on our way to our destination. We should be able to easily shelter ourselves, our animals, and our servants in this cave and have ample food for the night.&quot;<br /> GM: &quot;Difficulty 3&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically the player being able to declare very specifically what he's looking for allows the player to ensure he gets more of a reward for his roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:31:50-07:00","id":1083498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083492#post1083492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Randomly pulling a lion's den into existence out of nothing but plot isn't something you can do with survival alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of seems like it <i>should </i>be, though. I can't say I'm a big fan of requiring my players to spend XP on Charms before they're allowed to contribute collaboratively to the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:31:57-07:00","id":1083499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083488#post1083488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is... is Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm actually doing anything? Like, that looks a lot like something you should be able to just <i>do</i> with Survival, i.e., &quot;I'ma roll to find some useful fever-treating herbs that grow in the area, because I have Survival 3+.&quot; I'm kinda underwhelmed there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very situational, but if you spend a lot of time in different wilderness environments, or your Wits + Survival pool is bigger than your Intelligence + Lore pool, or you want to be able to introduce facts more than once per scene, it's pretty decent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:32:53-07:00","id":1083500,"title":"","content":"&quot;Rolling to find&quot; isn't the same as going &quot;Hey, there's a lion's den at the foot of this cliff. I roll to kick this guy I'm fighting into it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:33:31-07:00","id":1083501,"title":"","content":"I guess that because it's a introduce a fact, the difference is maybe that:<br /> Normal: &quot;I roll Wits+Survival to look for a herb in this forest to cure the rare poison my brother was given. I get 4 successes.&quot; ST: &quot;You're absolutely sure that no plant in this forest is suitable, but you know that it's in a different forest, far, far away.&quot;<br /> This charm: &quot;I roll Wits+Survival to declare that this forest has a super-rare herb in it that can cure my brother.&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Difficulty 4.&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;I succeed!&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Well done, you found a cure!&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, this charm is maybe one of those that lets you do something the rules don't technically allow (introduce a fact with Survival rather than Lore) but which a lot of STs would probably let you do anyway, tbh. I mean, in the above example, I probably would let people do, but technically you can't.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see my comments have already been made.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, overall I like these charms because they don't just let you do a human thing better, they actually let you do stuff a human can't do. They give you more options, and this makes them more interesting to play with, IMO.<br /> It's also interesting to see an Earth/Wood occult charm, Fire war charm, Earth larceny charm, Fire investigation charm, etc. We don't yet know yet how that'll work mechanically, but they do seem to work thematically sensibly. Hopefully it'll make playing an Earth-aspected detective and a Fire-aspected detective a bit different (unlike the previous edition), so make groups a bit more flexible (though I assume at higher levels, there'll be more crossover).<br /> <br /> Interestingly, I note that the Water-Presence charm has Fire-aspected prerequisites (I mean, Burning Passion Mien's got to be Fire).<br /> <br /> Oh, and finally, I think these charms are more mechanically clear than the ones in the Core book, which I found one of the major weaknesses of the Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:37:22-07:00","id":1083506,"title":"","content":"Yaaaay! Terrestrial previews!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:38:43-07:00","id":1083507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083488#post1083488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, cool, an anima Charm with a 1a cost. Don't remember offhand if we have any with a less-than-3a cost in the core.<br /> <br /> Is... is Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm actually doing anything? Like, that looks a lot like something you should be able to just <i>do</i> with Survival, i.e., &quot;I'ma roll to find some useful fever-treating herbs that grow in the area, because I have Survival 3+.&quot; I'm kinda underwhelmed there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're introducing a Fact with a Survival roll. Usually that's a Lore roll with a requirement of Lore 3+.<br /> Also, you're dictating the existence and location of a thing (within limits) instead of praying to the ST that whatever-it-is exists somewhere nearby maybe.<br /> <br /> e.g.:<br /> - The Anathema NPC is fleeing north, faster than you can keep up.<br /> - <span style=\"font-size:13px\">*rolls WWF* </span>No worries, there's a sharp cliff that way, known (and avoided) for its viper dens. We'll corner the demon and slay it; that is, if the vipers don't do our job for us.<br /> <br /> Without the Charm, the ST would just go &quot;uhh, that's up to me to decide, bro. no there isn't.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-25-2017, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:39:21-07:00","id":1083508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083499#post1083499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's very situational, but if you spend a lot of time in different wilderness environments, or your Wits + Survival pool is bigger than your Intelligence + Lore pool,</div> </div> </div> </div>In at least this case, for the cost of the Charm you could have bought another 2+ dots of Lore and solved the problem for good.<br /> <br /> I hear what folks are saying, and maybe some of this comes down to the rules for What Survival Actually Does being... vague, bordering on nonexistent? About all we have is that a roll &quot;is sufficient to take care of the necessities of life - food, water, shelter.&quot; Three successes is described as a difficulty &quot;which might daunt even heroes,&quot; such as &quot;plucking a gem from a nest of writhing serpents&quot; and well above surgery in the middle of a raging storm. Given all that, I would let three successes on a Survival roll find you basically sufficient food and shelter regardless, and I'd probably let you <i>functionally</i> declare facts with Survival regardless of whether you had the Charm or not.<br /> <br /> As Ferryman says, what is Survival supposed to be doing, if it's <i>not</i> letting you say, &quot;Yeah, I have food and shelter and medicine and comfort and etc., and I can locate setting-appropriate animals when need be&quot;?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083501#post1083501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that because it's a introduce a fact, the difference is maybe that:<br /> Normal: &quot;I roll Wits+Survival to look for a herb in this forest to cure the rare poison my brother was given. I get 4 successes.&quot; ST: &quot;You're absolutely sure that no plant in this forest is suitable, but you know that it's in a different forest, far, far away.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the former falls more into &quot;slap your ST&quot; territory for me - like you say, I don't think I'd have handled it that way in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 04-25-2017, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:40:23-07:00","id":1083509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083499#post1083499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's very situational, but if you spend a lot of time in different wilderness environments, or your Wits + Survival pool is bigger than your Intelligence + Lore pool, or you want to be able to introduce facts more than once per scene, it's pretty decent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think whether you like the Charm will depend heavily on whether or not you think that this is the sort of thing that should demand a Charm purchase. A Charm purchase is a significant investment. It should be <i>plainly </i>obvious what the added value of that purchase is. If there's debate over what that added value is, IMO that's probably a good sign that either A) the Charm isn't written clearly enough or, B) it's not doing enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:45:27-07:00","id":1083513,"title":"","content":"Being able to introduce a fact with Survival goes beyond just substituting a dot rating; it also means being able to boost the roll with Survival Charms. Remember that DBs don't get excellencies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1077496#post1077496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dragon-Blooded don't get free access to Excellencies. They don't get Excellencies at all, in fact. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1077519#post1077519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Basically, once we cut free Excellencies, and you had to buy one anyway, it opened up a lot of design to have a dice adder tailored to each Ability's specific needs, instead of using one generic template. The First Edition way of doing them, essentially, which has some significant benefits. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  added citations 04-25-2017, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:52:38-07:00","id":1083516,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Being able to use one Ability for a narrow application of another Ability is a thin and unconvincing justification for the purchase of a Charm. I've seen the argument made before and find it just as unpersuasive now.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not down on this preview as a whole. I'm excited for Terrestrial Charms (you have no idea). But a couple of these seem a little uninspiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:52:49-07:00","id":1083517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083513#post1083513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that DBs don't get excellencies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to introduce facts with survival would still be useful if they did. Not everyone has Lore charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:53:15-07:00","id":1083518,"title":"","content":"Well, as previously stated, it all depends on what you allow baseline Survival to do. As an ST, you can declare that, regardless of a Survival rating or success on a roll, there is absolutely no food/shelter/medecine in a certain area. This Charm lets the player say there is.<br /> <br /> It's value definitely varies according to table, as most things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:54:15-07:00","id":1083519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083517#post1083517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being able to introduce facts with survival would still be useful if they did. Not everyone has Lore charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or even Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:59:13-07:00","id":1083522,"title":"","content":"Well those are some really fun charms, gotta say that I found the salt-warding and storage ones to be my favourites just for how creative and thematic they are. Also I could see like a billion plot hooks and even setting ideas from Dragon's Hidden Treasure alone! Also points for now giving Occult-inclined DBs reason to carry salt around like proper exorcists!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:01:17-07:00","id":1083523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083518#post1083518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as previously stated, it all depends on what you allow baseline Survival to do. As an ST, you can declare that, regardless of a Survival rating or success on a roll, there is absolutely no food/shelter/medecine in a certain area. This Charm lets the player say there is.<br /> <br /> It's value definitely varies according to table, as most things.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is something that makes me inherently a bit uncomfortable. As an ST, if I declare that regardless of Survival rating or success on a roll there is absolutely none of that stuff, it's probably because the story I have in mind demands this. Case in point: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>'s example of the herb needed to cure his brother's illness. Okay, so that sounds great in theory but...in reality, if I intended to send my player to another forest far, far away to adventure in order to save his brother's life it's because <i>that was a cool story to tell</i>. If the player can then say &quot;Nah I got a Charm that says it's right here&quot; then as an ST I am faced with an unwelcome choice:<br /> <br /> Option 1: &quot;Nah bro, your Charm doesn't work for Plot Reasons. Now pack up and go where the story goes.&quot; (Player is extremely unhappy because his Charm purchase feels wasted)<br /> Option 2: &quot;Oh. Okay. That works. Uh, I guess we're done for today fellas. See you next week.&quot; (Everyone is unhappy because story ends prematurely and we're here to play the game, right?)<br /> <br /> This is why the rules for Introducing a Fact specifically state that the ST always has the final say, so as to preserve Plot Necessities. It's a neat mechanic, but there are inherent risks to building too heavily around it. This is particularly true for Charms, which are significant purchases that the players will (very reasonably) expect to be reliably useful to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:02:44-07:00","id":1083524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083518#post1083518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as previously stated, it all depends on what you allow baseline Survival to do. As an ST, you can declare that, regardless of a Survival rating or success on a roll, there is absolutely no food/shelter/medecine in a certain area. This Charm lets the player say there is.<br /> <br /> It's value definitely varies according to table, as most things.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It also depends on what the survival tree is about. Presumably, if there's a fact-introducing Charm in there, it means that there's some amount of terrain-control magic happening that would allow you to do things that Lore alone wouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083516#post1083516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Being able to use one Ability for a narrow application of another Ability is a thin and unconvincing justification for the purchase of a Charm. I've seen the argument made before and find it just as unpersuasive now.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">*shrug*</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Solar Stealth allows you to roll Dex + Stealth to join battle and grows into an awesome tree from that. That you find it to be thin and unconvincing is a problem others don't have.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-25-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:13:53-07:00","id":1083527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083523#post1083523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this is something that makes me inherently a bit uncomfortable. As an ST, if I declare that regardless of Survival rating or success on a roll there is absolutely none of that stuff, it's probably because the story I have in mind demands this. Case in point: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>'s example of the herb needed to cure his brother's illness. Okay, so that sounds great in theory but...in reality, if I intended to send my player to another forest far, far away to adventure in order to save his brother's life it's because <i>that was a cool story to tell</i>. If the player can then say &quot;Nah I got a Charm that says it's right here&quot; then as an ST I am faced with an unwelcome choice:<br /> <br /> Option 1: &quot;Nah bro, your Charm doesn't work for Plot Reasons. Now pack up and go where the story goes.&quot; (Player is extremely unhappy because his Charm purchase feels wasted)<br /> Option 2: &quot;Oh. Okay. That works. Uh, I guess we're done for today fellas. See you next week.&quot; (Everyone is unhappy because story ends prematurely and we're here to play the game, right?)<br /> <br /> This is why the rules for Introducing a Fact specifically state that the ST always has the final say, so as to preserve Plot Necessities. It's a neat mechanic, but there are inherent risks to building too heavily around it. This is particularly true for Charms, which are significant purchases that the players will (very reasonably) expect to be reliably useful to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from, but that is the deal with the whole &quot;introduce a fact&quot; shtick.<br /> <br /> It surely tests the ST's flexibility and ability to roll with it. Any kind of power that gives the player an opportunity to create part of the world outside of their characters will stress pre made stories.<br /> <br /> In the case you cited if you really wanted to have the player go to the other forest you could stage an encounter where the herb patch in this forest is ruined or inaccessible for some reason. It is good to keep your players' powers in mind before leaning too heavily on something that must happen for a story to work.<br /> <br /> That is really very general. Maybe you needed the prince alive but player with Archery Charm headshotted him from 3 miles away. Maybe you needed the girl who stole the gem to be thought of as innocent, but damn Investigation Charms...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:33:30-07:00","id":1083537,"title":"","content":"Pure awesome. The Charms are all nicely straightforward. The only one I was left wondering about was Following the River's Course. By money, I assume this means currency only. It would not affect a trade negotiation based on favors, or barter or anything other than actual, hard currency? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:40:42-07:00","id":1083540,"title":"","content":"I like the Charms, but oddly am not as enthused by this blog as I thought I would be. I more thought we were going to get something that's a bit more &quot;Design and development&quot;-y, that described some of the reasoning of structure and more ideas on how the elements worked and then examples to demonstrate it.<br /> <br /> I guess while I like it, it's a tad just spoiler-dumping and less what I kinda expected out of a blog post detailing thigns. Still neat stuff, though and interesting thematics. I like the ghsot-warding Charma lot myself.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:41:42-07:00","id":1083541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083527#post1083527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case you cited if you really wanted to have the player go to the other forest you could stage an encounter where the herb patch in this forest is ruined or inaccessible for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the fact introduced is immediately rendered unusable, how is this functionally different from declaring the Charm worthless in this situation? I don't know about you, but my players are bright enough to see through (and be irritated by) such a transparent bait-and-switch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083527#post1083527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is good to keep your players' powers in mind before leaning too heavily on something that must happen for a story to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you are coming from, but I'm sure that you can appreciate there is a significant difference between anticipating a character's ability to fire an arrow a long distance and the ability to <i>invent truths on the spot</i>. I think you'll agree that it's a little disingenuous to suggest that the latter is something that can be prepared for ahead of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:43:22-07:00","id":1083542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083540#post1083540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Charms, but oddly am not as enthused by this blog as I thought I would be. I more thought we were going to get something that's a bit more &quot;Design and development&quot;-y, that described some of the reasoning of structure and more ideas on how the elements worked and then examples to demonstrate it.<br /> <br /> I guess while I like it, it's a tad just spoiler-dumping and less what I kinda expected out of a blog post detailing thigns. Still neat stuff, though and interesting thematics. I like the ghsot-warding Charma lot myself.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I think the blog post didn't mention is that it is part 1 of 3. <br /> <br /> Part 2 will discuss the Elemental Aura mechanic that all these aspect keywords tie into, while Part 3 will discuss Elemental Signature Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":27}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:47:21-07:00","id":1083545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083542#post1083542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think the blog post didn't mention is that it is part 1 of 3.<br /> <br /> Part 2 will discuss the Elemental Aura mechanic that all these aspect keywords tie into, while Part 3 will discuss Elemental Signature Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww yeeaah \u266a<br /> [<span style=\"font-size:13px\">Edit: </span>spoilered for size I didn't think it'd be that big x_x]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/FhC19FC3Zr55u/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:47:31-07:00","id":1083546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083541#post1083541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you are coming from, but I'm sure that you can appreciate there is a significant difference between anticipating a character's ability to fire an arrow a long distance and the ability to <i>invent truths on the spot</i>. I think you'll agree that it's a little disingenuous to suggest that the latter is something that can be prepared for ahead of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>how is that different then the way <i>all</i> state fact charms work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:50:52-07:00","id":1083549,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with most of these. There's nothing particularly wrong with any of them, I would just need to see them in the context of a wider set in order to get a firm handle.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiding things in stone is a neat trick, but not very flashy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's all about the presentation. One adds pizzazz by hiding something in a particular place for a particular time and then pulling them out on people who weren't prepared for them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083488#post1083488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, that looks a lot like something you should be able to just <i>do</i> with Survival</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would say it's sufficiently outside of the description of the Ability in the core, and whatever is left should be set aside for the benefit of Lore.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's not my favourite Charm, but only because I feel as though it's not necessarily worth it to substitute just buying Lore, and even that is a low concern if I keep myself on point with Abilities as depictions of specific characters rather than calculated utilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:19:31-07:00","id":1083563,"title":"","content":"Reading the Unspoken Word feels more like a Presence or Larceny charm than Linguistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:29:52-07:00","id":1083570,"title":"","content":"This seems really cool to me! I'm excited to see how Dragon-blooded charms seem to feel much more elemental than I was expecting. I think that's going to be a core part of Sworn Brotherhood/mixed circle campaigns, and it looks like it's coming off well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:30:30-07:00","id":1083571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083542#post1083542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think the blog post didn't mention is that it is part 1 of 3.<br /> <br /> Part 2 will discuss the Elemental Aura mechanic that all these aspect keywords tie into, while Part 3 will discuss Elemental Signature Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, there we go. That does clarify things a bit there, yeah.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:36:46-07:00","id":1083574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083508#post1083508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In at least this case, for the cost of the Charm you could have bought another 2+ dots of Lore and solved the problem for good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that the roll for introducing a fact is <b>Intelligence</b> + Lore. This lets you use <b>Wits</b> + Survival. That means that even if you spent the 9 xp to up Lore from 0 to 3, then the character would still benefit from using this charm if their Wits was higher than their intelligence, and Attributes are not easily purchased. <br /> <br /> Also, I think everyone's forgetting that the storyteller has the ability to veto any fact introduction. So yeah I'm thinking this charm's primary function is to<br /> <br /> 1) Give the player an increased say in what the outcome his or her (Wits + Survival) roll produces<br /> 2) Allow to break the once per scene limit on fact introduction within the limits of the charm<br /> 3) Allow non-intellectual character builds to interact with Lore system in a limited capacity.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:39:23-07:00","id":1083575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083522#post1083522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also I could see like a billion plot hooks and even setting ideas from Dragon's Hidden Treasure alone!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;By the Dragons... The pendent is in Grandmother's GRAVESTONE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:41:41-07:00","id":1083579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083575#post1083575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;By the Dragons... The pendent is in Grandmother's GRAVESTONE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;So... Did anyone ever think to check the Scarlet Throne for the keys to the Imperial Manse?&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;....&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:45:15-07:00","id":1083583,"title":"","content":"Now I'm picturing Terrestrial Architects just *stuffing* their architecture with weapons. ALL the weapons; stuffed to the brim with 'em. So that its residents can just touch a wall or column and pull out a sword in case of a surprise raid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:46:14-07:00","id":1083584,"title":"","content":"Hm, I have mixed feelings here. On the one hand, minus a few nitpicks, the charms are all pretty clear in what they're supposed to do, and the difference between fluff and crunch is very clear, which is a huge positive. We also see some [Ability] 3, [Essence] 2 charms, which I don't think happened much, if at all, in the Solar charmset, which is a nice design space to hit.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, only a couple of charms really stood out to me as &quot;Yeah, I want to play a character that can do <i>that</i>.&quot; And none of the powers that make me think that are Essence 1, and since DBs don't get Supernal, that leaves me a little unenthused for building a starting character. I tend to agree that Wild-Wandering Forester feels like, while it's maybe a touch more powerful than what Survival can do on its own, it's not 8-10 XP more powerful. Also, Deep-Listening Palm feels <i>extremely</i> weak. Keen Hearing and Touch Technique is cheaper and <i>vastly</i> more powerful. If Dragon-Blooded are supposed to be &quot;Underdogs, but still a viable opponent for a Solar&quot; as has been stated, that charm sure doesn't show it.<br /> <br /> Back on the positive, Dragon's Hidden Treasure and Reading the Unspoken Word pretty quickly set my mind to working of all the cool things I could do with them (though RtUW need a little more clarification, as noted elsewhere).<br /> <br /> So, on the whole, not bad, but I really hope parts 2 and 3 can really ignite some excitement in me, because this didn't quite get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:56:01-07:00","id":1083592,"title":"","content":"What does the Earth/Air/Water/Heart keyword actually do?<br /> <br /> The charms are a solid blend of interesting and flavorful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:57:55-07:00","id":1083595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083584#post1083584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Also, Deep-Listening Palm feels <i>extremely</i> weak. Keen Hearing and Touch Technique is cheaper and <i>vastly</i> more powerful. If Dragon-Blooded are supposed to be &amp;quot;Underdogs, but still a viable opponent for a Solar&amp;quot; as has been stated, that charm sure doesn't show it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally really liked it, but on a re-read confused fluff with crunch. I'd clocked it as &quot;the thing you're touching is now your ear&quot;, which will allow the DB to hear round corners, up floors etc. But it's not. I sense a house-rule coming on if it reaches print like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","user":"Xerxes","date":". 05-10-2017, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:06:47-07:00","id":1083602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083595#post1083595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally really liked it, but on a re-read confused fluff with crunch. I'd clocked it as &quot;the thing you're touching is now your ear&quot;, which Wii allow the DB to hear round corners, up floors etc. But it's not. I sense a house-rule coming on if it reaches print like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does &quot;hearing as though it wasn't there&quot; not allow you to hear around corners or up floors?<br /> <br /> Also it's not really fair to compare it to Keen Hearing Tech. Keen Hearing is a second charm, Deep-Listening Palm is a first; Sensory Acuity Prana (a first Awareness charm) doesn't boost your ability to hear through things (beyond doubling 9s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:09:21-07:00","id":1083604,"title":"","content":"Are abilities still tied to elemental aspect?<br /> <br /> The Larceny charm is key'd for Earth, but Larceny isn't associated with Earth generally. Is it that Larceny is a Caste ability for Water Aspects, but an Earth DB could also treat this Charm as a caste one? But the Survival one is key'd for Wood, and there'd be no need to state that if it were natively Wood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083595#post1083595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally really liked it, but on a re-read confused fluff with crunch. I'd clocked it as &quot;the thing you're touching is now your ear&quot;, which Wii allow the DB to hear round corners, up floors etc. But it's not. I sense a house-rule coming on if it reaches print like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to hear as though the barrier wasn't there would allow you to hear through floors and around corners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:11:26-07:00","id":1083605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083602#post1083602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does &amp;quot;hearing as though it wasn't there&amp;quot; not allow you to hear around corners or up floors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the distance is still there. If you're at the bottom of a thirty-foot stone tower wanting to hear the whispered conversation going on at the top, the charm as written won't help. But what I thought it did (make the material act as your ears) places your heating much closer to the source, effectively enhancing your hearing as well as removing barriers to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:11:31-07:00","id":1083607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083592#post1083592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the Earth/Air/Water/Heart keyword actually do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance says in post 31 that that is information for the next preview.<br /> <br /> My speculation is that Elemental Aura will have a certain notion of needing to keep elemental energy accumulated around oneself balanced in a way that doesn't cause problems, but could also be built up in a manner that has benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:17:46-07:00","id":1083611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083602#post1083602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it's not really fair to compare it to Keen Hearing Tech. Keen Hearing is a second charm, Deep-Listening Palm is a first; Sensory Acuity Prana (a first Awareness charm) doesn't boost your ability to hear through things (beyond doubling 9s).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it should be as powerful as KH&amp;T, but it falls, way, way short. Even if we compare against Sensory Acuity Prana, SAP is the same cost, but is reflexive, covers all five senses, boosts JB rolls, and with any reasonable Awareness pool I would expect Double-9s to get me to hear through a wall with some ability. KH&amp;T is one charm deeper in the tree, but does everything DLP palm does, at 2m cheaper, reflexive, plus auto-succeed on diff 2 rolls, gives -1 diff, +1 auto-success, boosts even further with a relevant specialty, and applies all of those benefits to touch as well. Yes, KH&amp;T should be more powerful, both for being a Solar charm and for being one deeper in the tree, but that just feels like way too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:39:05-07:00","id":1083617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083604#post1083604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are abilities still tied to elemental aspect?<br /> <br /> The Larceny charm is key'd for Earth, but Larceny isn't associated with Earth generally. Is it that Larceny is a Caste ability for Water Aspects, but an Earth DB could also treat this Charm as a caste one? But the Survival one is key'd for Wood, and there'd be no need to state that if it were natively Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, while Abilities are still associated with Aspects, Charm trees for an Ability can have Charms aligned to different Aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:55:54-07:00","id":1083625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WhirlwindMonk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hm, I have mixed feelings here. On the one hand, minus a few nitpicks, the charms are all pretty clear in what they're supposed to do, and the difference between fluff and crunch is very clear, which is a huge positive. We also see some [Ability] 3, [Essence] 2 charms, which I don't think happened much, if at all, in the Solar charmset, which is a nice design space to hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point. I often feel that Exalted characters tend to be a bit min-maxed, all 5s and 0s, and it can be a bit ridiculous. This is encouraged by various things, but one of them is that so many charms need 4 or 5 in the ability, even charms near the beginning of the tree. Obviously you ought to expect 5s for charms deep into the tree, but I'd like to see characters who have 3 in an ability, and 2-3 charms, because having 3 in an ability is actually very high, as people in Creation go.<br /> <br /> Arguably it maybe doesn't make so much sense for Solars: if Solar charms represent Solar arete, and are extensions of their abilities, then maybe it does make sense that you can't, say, run on water unless you're a really good athlete.<br /> But DB charms are (while still having an aspect of arete of course) more being able to do things in a supernatural (elemental) way. So it maybe fits more for a DB who's a bit more keen-eared than average to also be able to hear through walls.*<br /> <br /> Though admittedly a lot of these example charms still require 5s, so we'll see.<br /> <br /> *I know no-one else seems to have mentioned it, but the fact that DB charms all seem to be allowing you to do something humans can't do, rather than doing something humans can kind of do but much better, is something I'm very happy to see.<br /> <br /> If that's the case amongst most DB charms, I'm seriously tempted to retire my 375xp Solar and play a 375xp Dragonblood instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:02:28-07:00","id":1083628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083604#post1083604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are abilities still tied to elemental aspect?<br /> <br /> The Larceny charm is key'd for Earth, but Larceny isn't associated with Earth generally. Is it that Larceny is a Caste ability for Water Aspects, but an Earth DB could also treat this Charm as a caste one? But the Survival one is key'd for Wood, and there'd be no need to state that if it were natively Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>While they said they'd explain some of this stuff later, Vance did, I think, say previously that the Aspects had the same abilities as 2nd ed (in response to someone asking if MA would be Earth-aspected like in 1st ed).<br /> Which implies that the xp and bp cost of ability dots at least are still tied to elemental aspect. But maybe the charms are not?<br /> Or maybe it's something like you favour all the charms in your aspect's ability and all the charms in your aspect?<br /> Or maybe you favour (as in cost) the charms in your ability, and the element of the charm is related to something else entirely?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part 2 will discuss the Elemental Aura mechanic that all these aspect keywords tie into, while Part 3 will discuss Elemental Signature Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me wonder if the aspect keywords are related to anima banners/flare. It would seem a bit complex to have an &quot;Elemental Aura&quot; and a seperate anima flare system.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, rampant speculation time? Maybe charms in your aspect don't flare your anima, and those out-of-aspect do? Or maybe vise-versa!<br /> That's probably a bit silly though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:08:55-07:00","id":1083631,"title":"","content":"How about<b></b>: Charms with your aspect contribute to your anima and DB animas are more powerful/useful than last edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:16:28-07:00","id":1083634,"title":"","content":"I'd like &quot;You may purchase charms of your aspect as if your Essence was 1 higher&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:32:55-07:00","id":1083651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083499#post1083499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's very situational, but if you spend a lot of time in different wilderness environments, or your Wits + Survival pool is bigger than your Intelligence + Lore pool, or you want to be able to introduce facts more than once per scene, it's pretty decent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also depends on how the Lore and Survival dice adders work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:36:03-07:00","id":1083656,"title":"","content":"Having opened with some critique, I do want to second the statement that it's cool to be able to see some idea of where DBs are going, and I <i>really</i> appreciate presenting some of the stuff (and even some systems!) here for public opinion. That's a cool thing.<br /> <br /> I'll also second that the cleaner language is a welcome change, and a good sign for DBs as a whole. This is, overall, pretty encouraging.<br /> <br /> It does seem like some of the problem with the Survival Charm is just the extreme vagueness as to what Survival can actually do, at what difficulty, with what degree of player input. I'll agree with Whirlwindmonk, here: I see some value, but it looks like a Charm I'd rate pretty hard as a speedbump, given the way I've always assumed Survival stuff was handled. For a ST who was much more restrictive as to what Survival could and couldn't do, it'd probably be more useful. As others have noted, though, STs still get veto rights over fact declarations; this is still a, &quot;Hey, with four successes, can I say I find...?&quot; - and in almost all situations I can think of, that's something I'd let them do with Survival already.<br /> <br /> On a more positive note, as others have said, embedding your sword in a physical object for safekeeping is really, really cool, and opens a lot of fun possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:10:30-07:00","id":1083680,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that it's a problem with Survival <i>per se </i>as it is that different tables have different assumptions for narrative authority. <br /> <br /> I've been in games where I can roll Wits+Skullduggery and a high success means I can say my PC knows of a chopshop nearby that's open. Heck, where I can say, &quot;My PC has 4 in Skullduggery; she probably knows a few chopshops around the city. Is there one nearby?&quot; and the answer will reliably be 'yes.'<br /> <br /> I've also been in games where the GM decides all these things and you can't add anything. Just roll to see if you know of what's already there.<br /> <br /> How powerful the Charm is depends on what you consider normal for your table.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:13:16-07:00","id":1083684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083656#post1083656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having opened with some critique, I do want to second the statement that it's cool to be able to see some idea of where DBs are going, and I <i>really</i> appreciate presenting some of the stuff (and even some systems!) here for public opinion. That's a cool thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! If there wasn't any criticism, that's when I'd be worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":22}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:15:16-07:00","id":1083687,"title":"","content":"So this is all pretty fantastic!<br /> <br /> Firstly I'll agree with wizard, it's great to see more DB charms being straight up supernatural stuff, which good because I've always been a bit suspicious of the line &quot;you'll know a DB charm because it's not a Solar charm&quot; which is incredibly vague and often very poorly explained. Even if the effect is very similar, the theme and subtle mechanical differences help. <br /> <br /> Also guys, remember that essence 1 DB charms are as weak as exalted charms ever get. They're supposed to be kind of underwhelming, just giving you a little boost or edge here and there. Now what you robably CAN do with them is what Solars do with their charms, and combo them into something huge. It's just when Solars do it they kill a whole wild hunt instantly, or something, whereas when DBs do it, if they work together, they might be able to fight Octavian or something epic.<br /> <br /> Again though, this is AWESOME and I like what I see a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:19:03-07:00","id":1083689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083634#post1083634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like &quot;You may purchase charms of your aspect as if your Essence was 1 higher&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's simple and straightforward. Which is why I'd have never thought of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:36:24-07:00","id":1083694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083684#post1083684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! If there wasn't any criticism, that's when I'd be worried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I do more than like this? Or give it multiple likes? I love you and your attitude Vance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:36:30-07:00","id":1083695,"title":"","content":"I think the flavor text of a lot of these charms could use more punching up for a final draft, just because it feels kind of barren and utilitarian and it'd be cool to get that majestic Prince of the Earth mood off of the Charms.<br /> <br /> I like the mechanics too, but it's hard to really get a sense of things because these charms are out of the context of the greater charmset. They all seem like fun effects.<br /> <br /> Excited for the next one to provide a little bit more context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:59:56-07:00","id":1083706,"title":"","content":"Just to second what Irked said, please let no one (particularly the writers) take my criticisms as coming from anywhere but a place of furious love. The simple existence of the preview makes me happy, and I'm looking forward to seeing more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083687#post1083687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're supposed to be kind of underwhelming</div> </div> </div> </div>Nooooooooooooo. I cannot disagree more. No. Nonono. Uh uh. Nnnnnnnope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:18:42-07:00","id":1083715,"title":"","content":"Dragon's Hidden Treasure makes me want to make a vigilante in a city who has &quot;back up plans&quot; stored in every building in the city. &quot;Where does she get those wonderful toys?&quot; I just like the imagery of that. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a> You have made me a happy person today.<br /> <br /> I like the whole pointing out the different aspects in the flavor as well. I like that dragon bloods now have means of keeping the restless dead at bay with cool thematic charms that enhance what used to be thaumaturgical wards. Will there be similar charms to keep Demons at bay? (with the whole &quot;The fact demon anathema can bypass this is one of the reasons they are super scary!&quot; kind of feel)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:34:17-07:00","id":1083721,"title":"","content":"I really love what I'm seeing in the preview.<br /> <br /> My favourite Charms are probably Deep-Listening Palm, Dragon's Hidden Treasure (I made my own variety at one point, but that was about accessing Elsewhere through representations of your Aspect element) and Following the River's Course. All of those spoke to me immediately with ideas of what you could do with them. I personally didn't thing the Essence 1 charms were underwhelming, although I admit that Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm is very table-dependent. I have a hunch I'd be the type to let my players suggest things like what the Charm does as a matter of course, because what kind of collaborative storytelling would it be if they didn't get to make statements about the world? Also I'm too lazy to some up with my own stuff. I don't see that as a problem, though.<br /> <br /> I saw some questions about Following the River's Course earlier. It might be my absolute favourite Charm in the preview, and I think that while it might not cover all the situations it'd be used in, it's still pretty clear. For me, I'd be willing to extend the Charm to cover both physical currency and bank transactions, provided the Terrestrial was personally present at the moment the payer (or perhaps an aide, I guess?) transferred the money. If the money is a large sum from multiple different sources, I'd limit the description to what I could reasonably make up about it, and unless I wanted to make a character moment or plot hook about something specifically, I'd only describe the general situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:40:35-07:00","id":1083724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083687#post1083687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also guys, remember that essence 1 DB charms are as weak as exalted charms ever get. They're supposed to be kind of underwhelming, just giving you a little boost or edge here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, these charms are a bit better than I expected, considering how weaksauce some of the DB charms in the Core were: for example, the charm that occasionally gave you +1 Resolve... or maybe, very occasionally +2 Resolve! Which might be good for DBs if they have no excellency, but in the Core they did, so it was just saving you a mote or 2 occasionally and that was it.<br /> <br /> These charms are better than that. The power level seems appropriate for low-essence DB charms to me, and I'm not someone who thinks DBs should be really weak (weaker than a Solar yes, but not really weak).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:49:11-07:00","id":1083727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083724#post1083724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, these charms are a bit better than I expected, considering how weaksauce some of the DB charms in the Core were: for example, the charm that occasionally gave you +1 Resolve... or maybe, very occasionally +2 Resolve! Which might be good for DBs if they have no excellency, but in the Core they did, so it was just saving you a mote or 2 occasionally and that was it.<br /> <br /> These charms are better than that. The power level seems appropriate for low-essence DB charms to me, and I'm not someone who thinks DBs should be really weak (weaker than a Solar yes, but not really weak).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I actually also think most of the low essence DB charms are more powerful than I would expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:55:43-07:00","id":1083730,"title":"","content":"The good:<ul><li>Compared to Solar charms, these are fewer words, yet have greater clarity. Awesome</li> <li>None of these are &quot;Solar charms, but not cool or powerful&quot;. I like the transferring your hearing thing. A creative player can take that places.</li> <li>Evocative effects all around. I can see some great emergent behavior coming from them in play.</li> </ul><br /> The not-so-good:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083488#post1083488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is... is Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm actually doing anything? Like, that looks a lot like something you should be able to just <i>do</i> with Survival, i.e., &quot;I'ma roll to find some useful fever-treating herbs that grow in the area, because I have Survival 3+.&quot; I'm kinda underwhelmed there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I am, but I think it really comes down to the ST. If a Survival-oriented player asked me to apply the Introduce a Fact rules to Survival, I would rule-of-cool it and not blink an eye. Other STs may not be so generous, in which case this is a powerful, if situational, effect. It reminds me of the outdoorsman archetype who defeats enemies through superior knowledge of his wilderness &quot;home&quot; rather than brute strength, and that's quite appropriate for Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:56:34-07:00","id":1083731,"title":"","content":"Something I greatly appreciate about the Charms? They reassured me that there IS literal elemental manipulation there in the set.<br /> <br /> I remember it coming up that the devs and writers wanted DBs to have more in their arsenal than just TLA Bending Tricks.<br /> <br /> To which my worry was that they might go too far in the other direction, giving us an Earth Aspect that can channel Integrity and Resistance of Earth to stand strong against the spear forged of pure malice from the Wyld... But can't actually use their mastery of Earth to form a rock wall for cover.<br /> <br /> These previews have COMPLETELY assuaged me of that worry. I mean we've got Fire Aspects stoking their anima to reinforce their troops, and we've got Earth Aspects literally sinking objects into the ground and rock, along with Water helping one change the passions of another. That stuff has <i>flavor</i>, and it's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T16:30:20-07:00","id":1083744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083715#post1083715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon's Hidden Treasure makes me want to make a vigilante in a city who has &quot;back up plans&quot; stored in every building in the city. &quot;Where does she get those wonderful toys?&quot; I just like the imagery of that.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZPkJcVLH0to\" data-code=\"ZPkJcVLH0to\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZPkJcVLH0to/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T19:16:07-07:00","id":1083781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083541#post1083541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the fact introduced is immediately rendered unusable, how is this functionally different from declaring the Charm worthless in this situation? I don't know about you, but my players are bright enough to see through (and be irritated by) such a transparent bait-and-switch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I see where you are coming from, but I'm sure that you can appreciate there is a significant difference between anticipating a character's ability to fire an arrow a long distance and the ability to <i>invent truths on the spot</i>. I think you'll agree that it's a little disingenuous to suggest that the latter is something that can be prepared for ahead of time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I think this is a very subjective, and somewhat thorny, subject to discuss. It all depends on how well you can hide your intentions and how well your players can read you, how forthcoming you are, how much do you care to be seen as railroading, how much your players care for being railroaded, etc...<br /> <br /> But the general system works like this:<br /> <br /> Att+Skill to attempt something. In this case a player can attempt to find food/shelter/medicine with Survival. The Storyteller says what, if anything is found. With the Charm the player can say what he finds. As with most things, with ST approval. The mechanical and narrative hook in which the Charm hangs is pretty clear.<br /> <br /> I think the general trend of the thread is that this is not a show stopper, but has it`s uses, how many and how often, depend on all those things mentioned above.<br /> <br /> I don`t agree that it is disingenuous to treat the powers differently. Why should it be easier for an ST to take into account that a player can kill people from a huge distance than to account that a player can declare Survival related facts about surrounding wilderness?<br /> <br /> Even if your player is antagonistically using the power &quot;against&quot; your planned development for the story, you can shift it. Say you are in the middle of the southern desert and the players need a flower that only grows by thermal pools of Mt. Harbek, one of the northernmost mountains to ever be explored.<br /> <br /> The player says &quot;BUT, I remember when hunting around this area as a child that I stumbled upon a grotto in an oasis that had JUST such flower&quot;<br /> <br /> As an ST you can just say &quot;Friend, I know you have that Charm and its super cool, and I promise you will get uses out of it, but this fact is contradicted by the fact I instituted earlier and will not fly&quot;<br /> <br /> That is a perfectly valid, sensible and amicable ruling.<br /> <br /> You can also evaluate if the northbound story can wait and develop the story from here. You can also say that for such a flower to grow so out of place, the grotto is probably very magical and dangerous. You can use it as a hook for creating a powerful place with powerful guardians to let them test their luck and achieve their goals, and maybe even greater treasure and glory, if they`re willing to play a high risk game.<br /> <br /> You can make up any other reason why they should head north.<br /> <br /> And here I go again delving into this...<br /> <br /> I`ll just say that I see its usefulness in games STed by me, and in the few (one) game where I play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 04-25-2017, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T19:20:51-07:00","id":1083786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083744#post1083744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZPkJcVLH0to\" data-code=\"ZPkJcVLH0to\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZPkJcVLH0to/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine a good stunt with that and the polemic Survival Charm?! I'd give out an Artifact for that, lol...<br /> <br /> &quot;Gramps used to tell all the time of a clearing in the Margrave Woods, where stood a lone boulder surrounded by faerie flowers where a great hero is rumored to have died and his fabled sword lost to time... OH SHIT!&quot;<br /> <br /> *Raises Tri-Sword above head!<br /> <br /> lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T20:52:51-07:00","id":1083806,"title":"","content":"My house rule is that any ability the person has rated at 3+ counts as part of their lore background, provided they have Lore at 3+. So the main benefit from the charm at my table would be the alternate dicepool and the fact that you might not have lore dots at all. Which, if you were a ranger style Wood aspect who was raised in a forest instead of the Realm, you might well not have any dots in Lore.<br /> <br /> I can see its utility, though I think a bit of errata to how Survival works for gathering food and finding random stuff might be useful too. I know I've seen complaints that Food Gathering Exercise is just how Survival should work normally, so some extra clarity there would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T00:04:33-07:00","id":1083878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083687#post1083687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also guys, remember that essence 1 DB charms are as weak as exalted charms ever get. They're supposed to be kind of underwhelming, just giving you a little boost or edge here and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that most new Characters will have nothing but E1 Vharms, and chargen in which all your options are underwhelming doesn't sound too fun.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be too pessimistic, especially based on such a small snapshot, though. I'm confident DBs will be fun to play, even if they haven't spoiled a Charm that makes me say &quot;wow, I want to make a character that uses that Charm&quot; yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T01:17:31-07:00","id":1083891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083695#post1083695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the flavor text of a lot of these charms could use more punching up for a final draft, just because it feels kind of barren and utilitarian and it'd be cool to get that majestic Prince of the Earth mood off of the Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might have over-corrected due to fan reaction to Charm prose in the core.<br /> <br /> I expect, at this point, they're not going to go through all the Charms and punch-up the flavor text. The emphasis is probably on showing they can make a leaner book with mechanical clarity and do so in a reasonable time frame.<br /> <br /> But I'm only guessing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T02:31:57-07:00","id":1083901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083634#post1083634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like &quot;You may purchase charms of your aspect as if your Essence was 1 higher&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how these keywords are distributed, that seems like something that could get very messy and convoluted to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bI feel as though these elemental Keywords and whatever this aura mechanic is on its own might be sufficient to fill the role of Supernal Ability in terms of a mechanic that interweaves with Charms in distinguishing Terrestrial Exalted. I don't think they'll need something to play around with Essence minimums.<br /> <br /> \u200bI even think that with this in mind, Aspect Abilities could be kept simple as the things for which one gets character creation and progression benefits, although there may be trends in which certain elements are more prominent in certain Abilities that lets whatever Aura is help to give Aspects a certain character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T02:47:07-07:00","id":1083902,"title":"","content":"If the elemental keywords are tied to how or when you may purchase them it raises questions about how multi-element charms work. The example we have changes based on whether you make your ghost repelling line out of salt or grain. Would someone who accessed it or got it cheaper due to their aspect be restricted to one or the other? <br /> <br /> We know that the Aura mechanic is supposed to replace out-of-aspect surcharges in functionality. Presumably that means it will have some mechanical effect on the charms themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:34:26-07:00","id":1083926,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to second (or third, or fourth) how cool it is to see the elements really playing a part in these DB charms. It's a very nice touch. I'd also, also like to second (or third, or etc.) how glad I am to see more openness in the development here. It's really encouraging and fun to see these design previews, and also to see criticism taken gracefully. While this particularly preview didn't do as much to get my imagination as I hoped, there are some really cool and solid effects in there (even Deep-Listening Palm is a good effect, I just think it's overpriced at 5m), and I fully expect the full and finished charmset will have plenty more and be a lot of fun to play. So thank you to the devs for these previews!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2324,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","user":"WhirlwindMonk","date":". 04-26-2017, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2324-whirlwindmonk","name":"WhirlwindMonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2324_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:33:37-07:00","id":1083985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083902#post1083902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the elemental keywords are tied to how or when you may purchase them it raises questions about how multi-element charms work. The example we have changes based on whether you make your ghost repelling line out of salt or grain. Would someone who accessed it or got it cheaper due to their aspect be restricted to one or the other?<br /> <br /> We know that the Aura mechanic is supposed to replace out-of-aspect surcharges in functionality. Presumably that means it will have some mechanical effect on the charms themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aura mechanic may not affect the charms; it might be that the charms create/affect your Elemental Aura (whatever that is; it sounds like it could be something similar to anima banner or flare. But perhaps not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how these keywords are distributed, that seems like something that could get very messy and convoluted to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you had a tree of charms with the same Elemental keyword it would be fine, but looking at those charms I'd guess that charms within a tree alternate in their elemental keywords (for example, there's a Water charm that has two prerequisites with rather Fire-sounding names).<br /> It might be a bit messy to reduce the essence prerequisites of the third, fifth and eighth charms in a tree by one.<br /> <br /> It might work, of course. I don't think it'd be terrible. But neither do I think it'd do all that much.<br /> <br /> Vance did say &quot;Only Solars(/Abyssals) get Supernal (and maybe Infernals have something similar?)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which made me think that probably getting +X essence for prerequisite purposes isn't something we're going to see in Dragonblood (or Lunars), though I'll admit it doesn't explicity say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:56:19-07:00","id":1084028,"title":"","content":"The two E1 charms seem fairly solid base level ones and the higher essence charms seem like they head into some fun places. Nice to see Passion Transmuting Nuance actually working for once, because that can be a hella useful effect if you've specced out for one particular type of Inspire actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:34:20-07:00","id":1084129,"title":"","content":"Given &quot;\u200bThe aspect of this Charm depends on which she uses\u2014salt is Earth, while grain is Wood.&quot; in the Occult ghost warding charm, that strongly implies to me that the elemental keyword can't relate to learning the charm, but is something that activates on use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:17:44-07:00","id":1084148,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% sure of that, since maybe you just have to use that option, but I can see what you mean there. It doesn't look like it's worded in the way where you buy the &quot;Earth&quot; version or the &quot;Wood&quot; version. Maybe the language is just misleading, but I think you're probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T11:28:32-07:00","id":1086268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1083475#post1083475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have liked to see one of their base dice adders, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur as I have some concerns as to how the possibility of variability might impact the approachablity of the splat and, by extension of their prominence, the game. I am hopeful the next previews will continue to build mounting excitement, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:26:46-07:00","id":1086333,"title":"","content":"Well, you'd really need to see 3 or 4 dice-adders if you're looking at their variability, and that'd be a pretty dull preview.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:24:46-07:00","id":1087176,"title":"","content":"Yeah, assuming that was all we saw in one of the previews.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll wait and see how many people house rule those charms into one, free excellency format. Especially considering how many house rules I already use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:36:59-07:00","id":1087179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1084129#post1084129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given &quot;\u200bThe aspect of this Charm depends on which she uses\u2014salt is Earth, while grain is Wood.&quot; in the Occult ghost warding charm, that strongly implies to me that the elemental keyword can't relate to learning the charm, but is something that activates on use.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. There are a few Charms where you do have to learn the elemental variants\u2014if you want to pick up multiple different kinds of Elemental Bolt, you'll need to pay 3xp for each additional one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:03:02-07:00","id":1087234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1087179#post1087179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's correct. There are a few Charms where you do have to learn the elemental variants\u2014if you want to pick up multiple different kinds of Elemental Bolt, you'll need to pay 3xp for each additional one.</div> </div> </div> </div>THAT is a number I can get behind. I disliked how dragon bloods basically had to pay for another charm just to get a minor alteration. Especially given they already had to pay more for their charms, to suddenly have to pay<br /> 10 or 12 XP to get an upgrade while plenty of charms for solars and lunars had 2 or 3 xp upgrades. Felt a bit unfair.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:08:36-07:00","id":1087236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083449-dragon-blooded-charm-previews?p=1087179#post1087179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's correct. There are a few Charms where you do have to learn the elemental variants\u2014if you want to pick up multiple different kinds of Elemental Bolt, you'll need to pay 3xp for each additional one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *rad airguitar*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:53:12-07:00","id":1087260,"title":"","content":"Concerning Wyld Wandering Forester's Charm, I think that it could be useful in a couple of aspects. First, it allows a DB to introduce a fact using Wits plus Survival, rather than Intelligence plus Lore, which suggests that some of the DB Charms will probably involve similar forms of substitution, allowing DB characters to be potentially very versatile (imagine the utility of a similar Melee Charm that allows a DB to replace Dexterity plus Thrown with Dexterity plus Melee when throwing a weapon that can also function as a melee weapon or a Thrown Charm that allows a DB to replace Dexterity plus Melee with Dexterity plus Thrown when wielding a weapon in melee combat that can also function as a thrown weapon). Second, it allows a DB to introduce a fact about the natural world of Creation without penalty (Lore seems to focus on introducing facts about the manmade world of Creation). Third, I think that an introduced fact would allow a DB to support another roll by reducing the difficulty of another roll (Medicine if the DB introduces a fact about a medicinal herb, Resistance if the DB introduces a fact about a hazard, etc), though we will have to see what other rules are introduced by the DB book before we know for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:20:17-07:00","id":1088776,"title":"","content":"So I was re-reading these DB charms (I have an essay on grammar to write, so obviously I'm finding ways to procrastinate), and I noticed this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spirit-Chaining Strike</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it does not become fully materialized, it is visible to all Dragon-Blooded characters in the scene, and can attack or be attacked by them as though it were material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then of course you have:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragon's Hidden Treasure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Charm can also be used to steal objects that other Dragon-Blooded have hidden using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, essentially, it doesn't matter which DB used the charm, it interacts with all DBs regardless (Dragon's Hidden Treasure of course works best for the DB who activated it, because they know where the item is; but any other DB who knew where it was could get it out).<br /> <br /> I wonder if this is going to be a general thing across the DB charmset, making them very good at co-operating with each other, but no more than anyone else with other Exalt types. But, at the same time, making them more vulnerable to each other if they don't work together (which, of course, in the Dynasty they don't do that well, as it's designed to keep them fighting each other instead of rising up against the Empress).<br /> <br /> This seems like a very elegant solution to &quot;how are DB charms cooperative&quot;, much more so than the 2nd ed cooperative charms which generally didn't work that well, or were that interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}